                text "Operator directive (2026-06-30): remove ALL global mutable state in the hfst library and eliminate the UB; no raw pointers unless absolutely necessary AND proven UB-free. Operator chose \"Everything — thread context through\" over keeping the safe data-bearing singletons. This SUPERSEDES the [dec:hfst:idiomatize-staging] deferral of symbol-coding de-singletonization to \"Stage 3+\". Landscape (measured): static mut = 0 already. Global mutable state populations: (A) data-bearing singletons — tropical symbol-coding NUMBER2SYMBOL/SYMBOL2NUMBER/MAX_NUMBER (~80 call sites across hfst_basic_transducer, both weight transducers, all convert_*, compose_intersect_*, hfst_basic_transition — the deepest change in the port), convert-format coding (NUMBER_TO_STRING/STRING_TO_NUMBER), diacritic registry (DIACRITIC_* — a deterministic memo-cache), exception slot (HFST_EXCEPTION — write-on-throw, ~0 real readers); (B) read-mostly config atomics in hfst_transducer.rs (CAN_MINIMIZE/ENCODE_WEIGHTS/MINIMIZATION_ALGORITHM/...); (C) per-compile scratch thread_locals (pmatch_compiler/xre/lexc_utils/twolc). Raw-pointer/UB landscape: 54 raw-ptr sites, genuine UB at WARNING_STREAM (leaked *mut Box<dyn Write> deref'd later) and HfstInputStream lifetime hole (open_hfst_input_stream returns *mut, erases the File borrow). Wave plan: warning-stream(UB) -> rawptr(convertible islands) -> convert-arena(convert.rs FST builder) -> input-stream(owned-File lifetime) -> scratch(thread_local->instance) -> small-globals(exception/diacritic/config) -> symbol-coding(KEYSTONE: thread coding context; has an internal fork — full &mut Context API param vs Rc<RefCell<Coder>> shared handle — resolve at that wave) -> gate. Each wave keeps 151 hfst tests green and commits separately."
